Fix window screensharing being frozen/black on Hyprland 0.56.0.

hyprwm/Hyprland PR #15991 ("output: add async commit scheduling for page
flips") moved the screenshare dispatch out of CMonitor's commit listener, where
it ran on every output commit, into COutputCommitCoordinator - and gated it on
`frame.copyFBPrepared`. That flag comes from CMonitor::needsACopyFB() ->
CScreenshareManager::outputCopyFBState(), which only counts SHARE_MONITOR and
SHARE_REGION sessions/frames, because only those read the output mirror FB.

Window captures re-render the window instead of reading the mirror FB, so they
never set copyFBPrepared, so CScreenshareManager::onOutputCommit() was never
called for them and CScreenshareFrame::copy() never ran. Effect: a
hyprland-toplevel-export-v1 client (xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland, i.e. Discord
"share a specific window") gets buffer/buffer_done, sends copy, and then never
receives ready or failed. Sharing a whole monitor kept working.

Dispatch onOutputCommit for every composed frame and hand the copyFBPrepared
flag to the manager, which skips only the monitor/region frames that actually
need the mirror FB.

